{
	title: 'Preserve the reading position through viewport reflow',
	spec: "On viewport reflow (including phone rotation and keyboard resizing), the transcript preserves its pre-reflow reading position. If only the top edge is within 40 CSS pixels, keep that exact top distance; if only the bottom edge is within 40 CSS pixels, keep that exact bottom distance. The threshold is inclusive. If neither or both edges are close, preserve the text character/row at the visible viewport midpoint at the new midpoint, accounting for changed wrapping and font metrics rather than preserving a scroll fraction or absolute scrollTop. Native caret/Range geometry provides a text anchor; non-text/blank areas use the nearest retained element and its relative position, and removed anchors fall back to a clamped content-center position. Impossible edge/center targets clamp to the available scroll range. Anchor state is captured before reflow and refreshed for deliberate scrolling, content changes and tab changes; resize-induced scroll events must not overwrite the pre-reflow anchor. Browser scroll anchoring must not compete with explicit restoration, and any running glide is canceled on resize. Native observers are cleaned up when the transcript unmounts; importing a module creates none. Browser tests verify exact/near top and bottom, the inclusive 40px threshold, middle text through width changes and both-near/short content cases, in both rotation directions. App width is capped by its layout container so a stale larger visual-viewport width cannot expand the layout viewport and trigger zoom when returning from landscape. Markdown high-water floors follow task fn's layout-local rule so obsolete height does not corrupt edge distances. Images that acquire intrinsic height after rendering preserve the pre-load reading anchor with the same edge/center rules, cancel a running glide, and refresh the anchor afterward. Capture-phase load listeners are removed on unmount. This also keeps a newly revealed deep-linked card in place without repeatedly forcing the reader back to it after deliberate scrolling.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Real bidirectional rotation caught stale --app-width feedback: a width of 844px carried into portrait made the layout/visual viewport remain 844px and zoom out. max-width:100% on App prevents that. It also caught Markdown streaming min-height retaining the portrait peak after wrapping changed; task fn now scopes peaks to width/font layout.',
		'Delayed image decoding changes scrollHeight without changing the transcript box dimensions, so the viewport ResizeObserver misses it. reflow.watch captures descendant load events and restores its cached reading anchor. The existing deep-link CDP regression reproduced 383px drift before the fix and less than 40px afterward.',
		'The 8y arrival card changes the geometry of the 41px near-edge rotation case: on landscape-to-portrait reflow its text-center target can lie above scrollTop=0. The browser assertion therefore verifies either the preserved character offset or clamping at the corresponding end of the scroll range, as the spec requires; demanding exact centering in that case is physically impossible.'
